A basic educational game loop usually looks like this:

```c++
int main() {
    // Initialize variables
    int score = 0;
    bool game_over = false;

    // Update loop
    while (!game_over) {
        // Handle input
        handle_input();

        // Update logic
        update_logic();

        // Draw
        render_screen();

        // Check for game over
        check_game_over();
    }

    // Clean up
    cleanup();

    return 0;
}
```

This keeps the core loop simple: update logic, draw, handle input, and clean up. You can add more complexity by adding AI, physics, or other features later.
